The attached image (Figure 2) illustrates the in vivo kinetics and biodistribution of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 nanoparticles after intramuscular injection in mice. Panel **a** shows whole-mouse imaging over 21 days, demonstrating Nano-11's retention at the injection site and gradual clearance. Panel **b** displays images of excised internal organs and injection sites at day 21, indicating no systemic distribution or accumulation in internal organs. Panel **c** quantifies the injection site fluorescence intensity over time, revealing a rapid initial decrease followed by a slower, sustained clearance, confirming Nano-11's ability to remain localized and avoid systemic distribution, crucial for its role as a safe and effective vaccine adjuvant.